-- title:
--   The ℤ̄ two-cusp lattice is spanned by the ℤ-integral set
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \ge 1$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ containing the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/M)^\times \to (\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$, i.e. such that every unit $u$ with $\mathrm{unitsMap}\,u = 1$ lies in $H$. Work in the space $S_2$ of weight-two cusp forms for the subgroup $\Gamma_H(M) \le \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$, defined as the image in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$ of the preimage of $H$ under the character $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ sending $\gamma$ to its lower-right entry mod $M$. For a subring $A \subseteq \mathbb C$, [`CuspForm.twoCuspIntegralSet M H 2 p A`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L54) is the set of $f \in S_2$ such that for every $t$ in the Hecke ring `heckeRingH M H 2` (the subring of $\mathbb C$-linear endomorphisms of $S_2$ generated by the Hecke generators `heckeGenH` with empty exclusion set), every Atkin–Lehner datum $W$ for $(M,p)$ (data $R$, $a$, $b$ with $M = pR$ and $pa - Rb = 1$) and every $n \in \mathbb N$, the $n$-th $q$-expansion coefficients of $t f$ and of $(t f)\mid_2 W$ both lie in $A$; `twoCuspLattice M H 2 p A` is its $A$-span. The assertion is the equality of subsets of $S_2$ $$\mathrm{twoCuspLattice}\,(M,H,2,p,\bar{\mathbb Z}) = \mathrm{span}_{\bar{\mathbb Z}}\bigl(\mathrm{twoCuspIntegralSet}\,(M,H,2,p,\mathbb Z)\bigr),$$ where $\bar{\mathbb Z}$ is the integral closure of $\mathbb Z$ in $\mathbb C$ and the inner integral set is taken with respect to the smallest subring $\bot$ of $\mathbb C$, namely the image of $\mathbb Z$.
--
--   This is the statement that the two-cusp lattice of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_H(M)$ commutes with the base change from $\mathbb Z$ to $\bar{\mathbb Z}$: the $\bar{\mathbb Z}$-lattice cut out by integrality of all Fourier coefficients of Hecke translates and of their Atkin–Lehner transforms is already generated by the forms whose corresponding coefficients are rational integers. It is used in the analysis of Atkin–Lehner pinning on the modular curve and in the production of an integral form with prescribed $U_p$-behaviour out of a member of the two-cusp integral set.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_twoCuspLattice_integralClosure_eq_span_twoCuspIntegralSet_bot.lean

